{{also|břėǵ|брег}}
==Albanian==

===Etymology===
Borrowed from a South Slavic language, compare {{cog|cu|брѣгъ||riverbank, hill}}, {{cog|sh|брег||hillock}} and {{cog|mk|брег||bank, shore, coast}}. Ultimately from {{der|sq|sla-pro|*bergъ||hill}}.<ref>{{R:sq:Topalli|page=243}}</ref><ref>{{R:sq:Orel|page=34}}</ref><ref>{{R:sq:Omari|page=109}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|sq|/bɾɛɡ/}}

===Noun===
{{sq-noun|m|brigje|bregu|brigjet}}

# [[coast]], [[shore]], [[riverbank]]
# [[dune]], [[hillock]]
# [[brink]]
# [[seaside]]

====Synonyms====
* {{l|sq|kodër}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|sq|bregore}}, {{l|sq|bregaloj}}, {{l|sq|bregale}}, {{l|sq|bregas}}
* {{l|sq|bregdet}}, {{l|sq|bregdetar}}

